<newsitem itemid="115366" id="root" date="1996-10-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: James Halstead year pretax profit higher.</title>
<headline>James Halstead year pretax profit higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		23.51		  vs 22.75</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.0		    vs n/a</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 9.25		   vs 8.5</p>
<p> Pretax		     10.63		  vs 10.32</p>
<p> Turnover		   77.64		  vs 72.67</p>
<p> Operating result	 10.71		  vs 10.50</p>
<p> Interest		   0.09 payable	 vs 0.18 payable</p>
<p> Tax			  3.44		   vs 3.43</p>
<p> Retained profit	  4.34		   vs 4.31</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 6</p>
<p>Div registration date  November 5  Ex-div date		October 28</p>
<p>NOTE - James Halstead makes flooring, motorcycle accessories, trailers, cabins and outdoor clothing.</p>
<p>It said it had bought German flooring distributor Objectflor Art &amp; Design Belags GmbH but did not give details.</p>
<p>Chairman Vincent Clare said in a statement that &quot;given reasonable trading conditions I expect further progress in the current year.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
